-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-write-014", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Achilleion in Thessaly is a tell of 200 by 260 m, layered from the Early and Middle Neolithic. Digs led by Marija Gimbutas uncovered pottery, bone tools, personal ornaments and stone tools."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-014 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Achilleion is in Thessaly [S1]; it is a tell of 200 by 260 m [S3]; it is layered (stratified) from the Early and Middle Neolithic [S3]; the excavations were led by Marija Gimbutas [S4]; the excavations uncovered pottery [S5]; the excavations uncovered bone tools [S5]; the excavations uncovered personal ornaments [S5]; the excavations uncovered stone tools [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-041 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Achilleion is a settlement site (a tell) in Thessaly, Greece (central claim: what kind of place and where) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; Achilleion is located in Thessaly, Greece [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The site is a tell [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The tell measures 200 by 260 m [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The tell is layered (stratified) and has Early Neolithic layers [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The tell is layered (stratified) and has Middle Neolithic layers [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The excavations (digs) were led by Marija Gimbutas [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The excavations uncovered pottery [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The excavations uncovered bone tools [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The excavations uncovered personal ornaments [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]; The excavations uncovered stone tools [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achilleion_(Thessaly)]"}]'::jsonb),
