pality of Palmela, Portugal [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castro_of_Chibanes]; A scarp guards the site on its south side [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castro_of_Chibanes]; The site was first occupied in about 2900 BCE [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castro_of_Chibanes]; The first occupants belong to the Copper Age (Chalcolithic) [SUPPORTED: https://www.cm-palmela.pt/viver/museu-e-patrimonio/patrimonio-cultural/patrimonio-arqueologico/castro-de-chibanes]; Its people farmed and kept livestock [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castro_of_Chibanes]; Its people gathered molluscs from the sea [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castro_of_Chibanes]"}]'::jsonb),
