vel, the Iron Age hillfort of Cadbury Castle looks down to the Exe Valley. Here Thomas Fairfax''s Parliamentarians camped while besieging Bickleigh Castle."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-015 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is some 250 metres above sea level [S3]; Cadbury Castle is an Iron Age hillfort [S1]; it looks down to the Exe Valley [S3]; Thomas Fairfax''s Parliamentarians camped here [S2]; they camped while besieging Bickleigh Castle [S2]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-044 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cadbury Castle (Devon, England, near Bickleigh) is an Iron Age hillfort [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cadbury_Castle,_Devon]; The site lies some 250 metres above sea level [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cadbury_Castle,_Devon]; It looks down to the Exe Valley [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cadbury_Castle,_Devon]; Thomas Fairfax''s Parliamentarian forces camped at the hillfort during the English Civil War [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cadbury_Castle,_Devon]; They camped there while besieging Bickleigh Castle [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cadbury_Castle,_Devon]; The siege of Bickleigh Castle was laid from Cadbury (Fairfax''s Parliamentarian troops attacked the castle) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bickleigh_Castle]"}]'::jsonb),
