', '1618054c13f81242f9a89bae21e4416b9b503e6ac89573ec9f30f7247fac927d', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-write-018", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "La Quemada developed between 300 and 1200 AD, its sunken patios and altar-pyramids all built of rhyolite slabs. A speculation of 1780 began the belief it is the mythical Seven Caves."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-018 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "La Quemada developed between 300 and 1200 AD [S5]; it has sunken patios and altar-pyramids [S6]; all its architectonic elements, including these, were built of rhyolite slabs [S7]; a speculation of 1780 began the belief that it is the mythical Seven Caves [S3, S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-verify-053 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "La Quemada is an archaeological site (a Mesoamerican ceremonial and settlement complex on a hill) in Zacatecas, Mexico [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Quemada]; La Quemada developed between 300 and 1200 AD [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Quemada]; The site has sunken patios and altar-pyramids [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Quemada]; All its architectural elements were built of rhyolite slabs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Quemada]; In 1780 a speculation (Clavijero associating the site with Chicomoztoc) was made [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Quemada]; That speculation originated the belief that La Quemada is the mythical Seven Caves [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Quemada]"}]'::jsonb),
