teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "In June 1992, four farmers drained five small ponds and found them to be large manmade caverns: the Longyou Grottoes, 24 sandstone chambers with ceilings up to 30 m high."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-018 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "in June 1992 the caves were found [S2]; four farmers found them [S2]; the farmers drained five small ponds [S2]; the ponds turned out to be large manmade caverns [S2, S3]; the Longyou Grottoes are 24 sandstone chambers [S1]; ceilings reach up to 30 m high [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-054 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Longyou Grottoes (also called Longyou Caves) are a group of artificial, man-made caverns in Longyou County, Quzhou, Zhejiang Province, China [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longyou_Caves]; There are 24 chambers [SUPPORTED: https://longyou-caves.cn/en]; The chambers are cut in sandstone [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longyou_Caves]; Ceilings are up to 30 m high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longyou_Caves]; The caverns were found in June 1992 [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longyou_Caves]; The finders were four farmers (Wu Anai and three companions) [SUPPORTED: https://longyou-caves.cn/en/discovery]; The farmers drained five small ponds (Wikipedia''s wording; the official site says they first drained one pond and nearby ponds followed) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longyou_Caves]; The ponds turned out to be large manmade caverns [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Longyou_Caves]"}]'::jsonb),
