l", "quote": "The Chalkotheke, whose name means bronze store, stood on the Athenian Acropolis. Its function is known only from 4th century BC inscriptions, one ordering all its objects listed on a stele."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-019 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the Chalkotheke''s name means bronze store [S1]; it stood on the Athenian Acropolis [S1]; its function is known only from 4th century BC inscriptions [S2]; one of these texts (a decree) orders all the objects stored in it to be listed [S2, S3]; the list was to be inscribed on a stele [S3]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-055 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Chalkotheke was a structure (a store) on the Athenian Acropolis, Greece [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkotheke]; The name Chalkotheke means bronze store [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkotheke]; Its function is known only from inscriptions (nothing survives that shows it otherwise) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkotheke]; The inscriptions that tell its function date to the 4th century BC [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkotheke]; One inscription (a decree) orders all objects stored in the Chalkotheke to be listed [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkotheke]; The list is to be inscribed on a stele erected in front of the building [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalkotheke]"}]'::jsonb),
