t/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Birkrigg Stone Circle sets 12 stones inside a ring of 20 on Birkrigg Common. Beneath its cobbled pavements lay five cremations, one covered by an inverted urn."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-check-020 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the circle has an inner ring of 12 stones [S2]; the inner ring sits inside an outer ring of 20 stones [S2]; the circle is on Birkrigg Common [S1]; the inner circle has cobbled pavements (an upper and a lower layer of cobbles) [S3]; five cremations lay beneath the pavements [S4]; one of the cremations was covered by an inverted urn [S4]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-01: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-01-verify-058 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-01/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Birkrigg Stone Circle is a Bronze Age stone circle on Birkrigg Common [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birkrigg_stone_circle]; The circle has an inner ring of 12 stones [SUPPORTED: https://co-curate.ncl.ac.uk/resources/view/108728/]; The inner ring of 12 stones is set inside an outer ring of 20 stones [SUPPORTED: https://co-curate.ncl.ac.uk/resources/view/108728/]; Beneath the circle lay cobbled pavements (an upper and a lower pavement of cobbles) [SUPPORTED: https://co-curate.ncl.ac.uk/resources/view/108728/]; Beneath the cobbled pavements lay five cremations [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birkrigg_stone_circle]; One of the five cremations was covered by an inverted urn [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birkrigg_stone_circle]"}]'::jsonb),
